Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 13:57:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(oci): pin safe_whiteout_dir component guards and
 missing-leaf tolerance

### What
Pins `safe_whiteout_dir` traversal rules: any non-Normal path component (`./`, `../`, absolute prefix) is rejected, while not-yet-existing normal directories are tolerated and an empty parent resolves to the extraction root.

### Why it matters
This guard is the security boundary keeping OCI whiteouts inside the rootfs. Accepting `Component::CurDir`/`ParentDir` would let a crafted layer walk out of the root; rejecting missing directories would break legitimate layers that create parents later. The existing symlink test only covers the symlink branch, so these mutations survive.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| accept all components (`_ => {}`) | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| treat NotFound as fatal | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-oci --lib safe_whiteout_dir_rejects_non_normal`.

Spec-Ref: OCI image-spec layer whiteout application (path traversal containment)

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-oci/src/lib.rs | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-oci/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-oci/src/lib.rs
index b2b2f97b..d5ac45bc 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-oci/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-oci/src/lib.rs
@@ -793,6 +793,23 @@ mod tests {
         fs::remove_dir_all(cache).unwrap();
     }
 
+    #[test]
+    fn safe_whiteout_dir_rejects_non_normal_components_and_missing_leaf_is_ok() {
+        let root = temp_dir("whiteout-components");
+        // parent with a CurDir component is rejected (non-Normal)
+        assert!(safe_whiteout_dir(&root, Path::new("./sub")).is_err());
+        // parent with ParentDir is rejected
+        assert!(safe_whiteout_dir(&root, Path::new("../escape")).is_err());
+        // absolute prefix is rejected
+        assert!(safe_whiteout_dir(&root, Path::new("/abs")).is_err());
+        // plain missing directories are tolerated (created later by the layer)
+        let ok = safe_whiteout_dir(&root, Path::new("fresh/deeper")).unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(ok, root.join("fresh/deeper"));
+        // empty parent resolves to the root itself
+        assert_eq!(safe_whiteout_dir(&root, Path::new("")).unwrap(), root);
+        fs::remove_dir_all(root).unwrap();
+    }
+
     #[test]
     fn blob_downloads_only_on_a_miss_and_repairs_verified_content() {
         let cache = temp_dir("repair");
